<|start|>assistant to=user<|message|># 詞: 銀包

1. 我個銀包唔見咗，入面仲有張八達通同埋啲現金。 (My wallet is missing, and it still has an Octopus card and some cash inside.)
2. 佢成日話自己唔使帶銀包出街，因為所有嘢都用手機支付。 (He always says he doesn't need to bring a wallet out because he pays for everything with his phone.)
3. 呢個銀包係我阿媽送畀我嘅生日禮物，用咗十年都仲好靚。 (This wallet is the birthday gift my mum gave me, and it's still in good condition after ten years.)
4. 佢喺巴士度俾人偷咗銀包，成個禮拜都悶悶不樂。 (He had his wallet stolen on the bus, and he's been gloomy for a whole week.)
5. 銀包入面除咗銀紙之外，仲有一張我同朋友嘅合照。 (Besides banknotes, there's also a photo of me and my friends in the wallet.)
6. 你唔好成日咁亂放銀包，搞到自己搵唔到錢。 (Don't keep putting your wallet in random places, or you'll end up not being able to find your money.)
7. 我新買咗個皮革銀包，摸落去好舒服。 (I bought a new leather wallet, it feels very comfortable to touch.)
8. 佢見到銀包跌咗喺地下，仲好有禮貌咁幫人執返起。 (He saw a wallet fall on the ground and politely helped pick it up for someone.)
9. 呢個銀包太細咗，放唔晒我啲咭同收據。 (This wallet is too small, it can't fit all my cards and receipts.)
10. 佢出街前一定要檢查銀包有冇帶齊身分證同信用卡。 (Before going out, he always has to check if his wallet has his ID and credit card.) [end of text]


